  abstract = {Neither the popular idea that were incorporated into one and there was no difference between and criminal laws nor the so called civil is pertinent to the ancient Chinese laws.For,the former means there were all kinds of in ancient China which were not disjoint,while the latter is just something of speciosity which blurs the differences between the and criminal laws,between the of ancient and modern times,and between the of China and the West.In the special historical conditions of ancient China,laws were merely tools for the rulers,the core of which is the word penalty.That is,all these are criminal in a broad sense.There existed only big or small crimes,heavy or light penalties which were relevant neither to law nor to criminal law where nobody tried to differentiate or criminal.This kind of could be called some unilateralist criminal law at most.In fact,there was no social basis for a law in ancient China,where the relationship or disputes between people were adjusted by the customary rituals and etiquettes.},
}

